    <statement><p>Find the equation of the sphere centered at <m>(-6, -4, -3)</m> with
radius 3.  Normalize your equations so that the coefficient of
<m>x^2</m> is 1.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
<p>Give an equation which describes the intersection of this sphere with
the plane <m>z = -2</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0002"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(x-\left(-6\right)\right)^{2}+\left(y-\left(-4\right)\right)^{2}+\left(z-\left(-3\right)\right)^{2}-9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(x-\left(-6\right)\right)^{2}+\left(y-\left(-4\right)\right)^{2}+1-9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
